 "applier": "mechanical-nominator",
 "rule": "narration-rule-v2-BLIND-AUTHORED.md +R-086/R-090 amendments",
 "n": 124,
 "declared_policies": [
  "P1 OBJECT = structural attachment ONLY (R-086): O-1/O-2/O-3 remain; O-4 (independent measure-noun frame) is DISABLED, because the amendment defines object as 'an argument attached to a detected comparator/threshold/direction'. Consequence: OBJECT can never be the sole firing element and therefore never changes the class.",
  "P2 ENUMERATIVE (R-090): >=1 element present => class=not_narration (FINAL); all four absent => class=nominee (escalates to human-style judgment; NOT a verdict of narration).",
  "P3 Plural folding PERMITTED and applied uniformly to the inventory NOUNS only (measure nouns O-4 [moot under P1], generic-process nouns D-O1, document nouns D-C1/D-D2): 'levels'~'level', 'values'~'value', 'examples'~'example'.",
  "P4 NO verb-inflection folding. Sec 1.4 forbids stemming/lemmatizing and the amendment extends folding only to inventory nouns. Only the exact listed surface forms fire. Consequences recorded as data: 'lose' (row 13) fires D-1 but 'losing' (row 5) does not; 'are in' does not match C-3 'is in' (row 90); 'expansive' does not match D-1 'expand' (row 90).",
  "P5 OQ-5 followed: unbound/unfilled operand slots keep COMPARATOR true but THRESHOLD false (rows 76, 91, 94).",
  "P6 Sec 3.2.1-3.2.3 followed: negation, modality, hypotheticals, definitions and quoted/illustrative material all count as surface presence.",
  "P7 T-4 anti-circularity policy (rule gap): T-4 quantity words (all/any/every/each/'no'+count-noun) fire only when filling the operand slot of an INDEPENDENTLY-detected comparator span. The O-2 attachment route cannot be satisfied by the candidate T-4 word itself, otherwise T-4 is self-licensing and vacuous. Affects rows 19, 53, 54, 66, 79, 98, 116.",
  "P8 Timeframe expressions ('5 minute', 'one minute', 'five-minute', '15minute', 'two-minute') are DURATION literals under T-3 and are NOT struck by D-T3, which strikes only calendar/clock POINTS ('9:30 a.m.', '9:45'). This is the single highest-firing threshold route in this corpus.",
  "P9 Nominal-hood for O-1/O-2/O-3: noun phrases and pronouns ('it') count (D-O2 lists only I/we/you/they/the team/the author/the reader/this document/the following/the above). Bare numerals, clock times and single-letter placeholders do NOT count as nominals (OQ-5 rationale). Adjectival modifiers ('lower lows', 'highest point') are NOT subjects or direct objects and so do NOT trigger O-3.",
  "P10 D-3 '-er/-est' is restricted to genuine comparative/superlative morphology; agentive/lexical -er words (order, buyers, filter, whether, either, after, retest, hammer, breaker, metatrader) are NOT comparatives. 'upper' IS counted as a comparative form.",
  "P11 No analogical extension (Sec 2 / 3.4.4): spans that 'feel' directional or relational but match no listed form are ABSENT. Recorded as data: 'to the upside' (row 33, 'upside' is not 'up'/'upward'), 'at max' (row 121, not 'at most'/'maximum of'), 'whichever you prefer' (rows 69/83, D-4 requires 'prefer X over Y'), 'low volume' (row 20, D-2 lists 'lower' not 'low'), 'a whole dollar level' (row 40, T-3 requires a currency SYMBOL or CODE plus a magnitude).",
  "P12 D-C1/D-D2 locative strikes apply only when the governed nominal is a document/discourse noun or deictic. Market-position uses of above/below/over/under/up/down are therefore NOT struck ('below vwap', 'come down to vwap', 'scroll down to oscillate')."
 ],
